{
  "title": "Other Aamal of the First Night",
  "data": "Acts of the Night\nHusband and wife are recommended to have intercourse tonight; it is otherwise disliked on the first night of a lunar month.\nPerform ghusl tonight.\nBathe in a flowing river, pouring thirty handfuls of water over the head.\nVisit the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.).\nBegin the [One Thousand Unit Prayers](AA4) of Ramazan tonight.\nPray two units, reciting in each [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-An'am](A10), then ask Allah for security against apprehensions and ailments.\nRecite [Dua Jawshan Kabir](E29).\nRecite [Dua Hajj](AA9).\nRecite [Sahifa Sajjadiya 44](AA48), Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)'s supplication for welcoming Ramazan.",
  "tabs": [
    "Allahumma Inna Hadha al-Shahr al-Mubarak\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنَّ هٰذَا الشَّهْرَ الْمُبَارَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA HAADHASH SHAHRAL MUBAARAK\nO Allah, this blessed month\nالَّذِي اُنْزِلَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنُ\nALLADHEE UNZILA FEEHIL QUR'AAN\nin which the Qur'an was revealed\nوَجُعِلَ هُدَىً لِلنَّاسِ\nWA JU'ILA HUDAA LIN NAAS\nand was made guidance for people\nوَبَيِّنَاتٍ مِنَ الْهُدَىٰ وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nWA BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nand clear proofs of the guidance, and the Criterion (of right and wrong),\nقَدْ حَضَرَ\nQAD HADAR\nhas commenced.\nفَسَلِّمْنَا فِيْهِ\nFASALLIMNAA FEEH\nSo, (please) keep us out of blemish during it,\nوَسَلَّمْهُ لَنَا\nWA SALLAMHU LANAA\nkeep it sound for us,\nوَتَسَلَّمْهُ مِنَّا فِيْ يُسْرٍ مِنْكَ وَعَافِيَةٍ\nWA TASALLAMHU MINNAA FEE YUSRIN MINKA WA A'AFIYAH\nand receive it from us with means of easiness and good health from You.\nيَا مَنْ اَخَذَ الْقَلِيلَ وَشَكَرَ الْكَثِيرَ\nYAA MAN AKHADHAL QALEELA WA SHAKARAL KATHEER\nO He Who has accepted the little (deed) and thanked for the much,\nاقْبَلْ مِنِّي الْيَسِيرَ\nIQBAL MINNIL YASEER\n(please) accept from me the little (deed).\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّي اَسْاَلُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUK\nO Allah, I beseech You\nاَنْ تَجْعَلَ لِي اِلَىٰ كُلِّ خَيْرٍ سَبِيلاً\nAN TAJ'ALA LEE ILAA KULLI KHAYRIN SABEELAA\nto make for me a path to every decency,\nوَمِنْ كُلِّ مَا لَا تُحِبُّ مَانِعاً\nWA MIN KULLI MAA LAA TUHIBBU MAANI'AA\nand to make for me a barrier against everything that You do not like.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nيَا مَنْ عَفَا عَنِّي وَعَمَّا خَلَوْتُ بِهٖ مِنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ\nYAA MAN A'FAA A'NNEE WA A'MMAA KHALAWTU BIHEE MINAS SAYYI'AAT\nO He Who has pardoned me and overlooked the misdeeds that I have committed secretly!\nيَا مَنْ لَمْ يُؤَاخِذْنِي بِارْتِكَابِ الْمَعَاصِي\nYAA MAN LAM YU'AAKHIDHNEE BIRTIKAABIL MA'AASEE\nO He Who has not punished me for my committing acts of disobedience to Him!\nعَفْوَكَ عَفْوَكَ عَفْوَكَ يَا كَرِيمُ\nA'FWAKA A'FWAKA A'FWAKA YAA KAREEM\nI seek Your pardon, I seek Your pardon, I seek Your pardon, O All-generous!\nاِلٰهِي وَعَظْتَنِي فَلَمْ اَتَّعِظْ\nILAAHEE WA A'ZTANEE FALAM ATTA'IZ\nO my God, You advised me, but I have not followed Your advice\nوَزَجَرْتَنِي عَنْ مَحَارِمِكَ فَلَمْ اَنْزَجِرْ\nWA ZAJARTANEE A'N MAHAARIMIKA FALAM ANZAJIR\nand You rebuked me for violating that which You have deemed forbidden, but I have not stopped.\nفَمَا عُذْرِي\nFAMAA U'DHREE\nNow, what is my excuse?\nفَاعْفُ عَنِّي يَا كَرِيمُ\nFA'FU A'NNEE YAA KAREEM\nSo, (please) pardon me, O All-generous!\nعَفْوَكَ عَفْوَكَ\nA'FWAKA A'FWAK\nI seek Your pardon, I seek Your pardon!\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّي اَسْاَلُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUK\nO Allah, I beseech You\nالرَّاحَةَ عِنْدَ الْمَوْتِ\nAR-RAAHATA I'NDAL MAWT\nfor rest at death\nوَالْعَفْوَ عِنْدَ الْحِسَابِ\nWAL A'FWA I'NDAL HISAAB\nand for pardon at calling to account.\nعَظُمَ الذَّنْبُ مِنْ عَبْدِكَ\nA'ZUMADH DHANBU MIN A'BDIK\nGreat is the sin of Your servant;\nفَلْيَحْسُنِ التَّجَاوُزُ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ\nFALYAHSUNIT TAJAAWUZU MIN I'NDIK\nso, let Your overlooking him be excellent.\nيَا اَهْلَ التَّقْوَىٰ وَيَا اَهْلَ الْمَغْفِرَةِ\nYAA AHLAT TAQWAA WA YAA AHLAL MAGHFIRAH\nO He Who is worth being feared and is worth forgiving!\nعَفْوَكَ عَفْوَكَ\nA'FWAKA A'FWAK\nI seek Your pardon, I seek Your pardon.\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّي عَبْدُكَ ابْنُ عَبْدِكَ ابْنُ اَمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'BDUKABNU A'BDIKABNU AMATIK\nO Allah, I am Your servant and the son of Your servant and Your she-servant\nضَعِيفٌ فَقِيرٌ اِلَىٰ رَحْمَتِكَ\nDA'EEFUN FAQEERUN ILAA RAHMATIK\nand I am weak and in need for Your mercy;\nوَاَنْتَ مُنْزِلُ الْغِنَىٰ وَالْبَرَكَةِ عَلَىٰ الْعِبَادِ\nWA ANTA MUNZILUL GHINAA WAL BARAKATI A'LAL I'BAAD\nwhile You are the Pourer of wealth and bless on the servants (of You),\nقَاهِرٌ مُقْتَدِرٌ\nQAAHIRUN MUQTADIR\nYou are omnipotent and full of power,\nاَحْصَيْتَ اَعْمَالَهُمْ\nAHSAYTA A'MAALAHUM\nYou have recorded all their (i.e. Your servants) deeds,\nوَقَسَمْتَ اَرْزَاقَهُمْ\nWA QASAMTA ARZAAQAHUM\ndecided the sustenance of each one them,\nوَجَعَلْتَهُمْ مُخْتَلِفَةً اَلْسِنَتُهُمْ وَاَلْوَانُهُمْ\nWA JA'ALTAHUM MUKHTALIFATAN ALSINATUHUM WA ALWAANUHUM\nand made them of different languages and colors\nخَلْقاً مِنْ بَعْدِ خَلْقٍ\nKHALQAN MIN BA'DI KHALQ\nin different stages of creation.\nوَلَا يَعْلَمُ الْعِبَادُ عِلْمَكَ\nWA LAA YA'LAMUL I'BAADU I'LMAK\nYour servants can never attain Your knowledge\nوَلَا يَقْدِرُ الْعِبَادُ قَدْرَكَ\nWA LAA YAQDIRUL I'BAADU QADRAK\nand Your servants can never recognize the real estimate that is due to You.\nوَكُلُّنَا فَقِيرٌ اِلَىٰ رَحْمَتِكَ\nWA KULLUNAA FAQEERUN ILAA RAHMATIK\nAll of us are needy for Your mercy.\nفَلَا تَصْرِفْ عَنِّي وَجْهَكَ\nFALAA TASRIF A'NNEE WAJHAK\nSo, (please) do not turn Your Face away from me\nوَاجْعَلْنِيْ مِنْ صَالِحِي خَلْقِكَ\nWAJ'ALNEE MIN SAALIHEE KHALQIK\nand include me with the virtuous creatures of You\nفِيْ الْعَمَلِ وَالْاَمَلِ\nFIL A'MALI WAL AMAL\nin deeds, hopes,\nوَالْقَضَاءِ وَالْقَدَرِ\nWAL QADAA'I WAL QADAR\nand Your decisions (for me).\nاَللَّهُمَّ اَبْقِنِي خَيْرَ الْبَقَاءِ\nALLAAHUMMA ABQINEE KHAYRAL BAQAA'\nO Allah, (please) keep me alive in the best manner of living,\nوَاَفْنِنِي خَيْرَ الْفَنَاءِ عَلَىٰ مُوَالاةِ اَوْلِيَائِكَ\nWA AFNINEE KHAYRAL FANAA'I A'LAA MUWAALAATI AWLIYAA'IK\ndecide for me to die in the best manner of death keeping loyal to Your representatives,\nوَمُعَادَاةِ اَعْدَائِكَ\nWA MU'AADAATI A'DAA'IK\nincurring the enmity of Your enemies,\nوَالرَّغْبَةِ اِلَيْكَ وَالرَّهْبَةِ مِنْكَ\nWAR RAGHBATI ILAYKA WAR RAHBATI MINK\nkeeping desiring for You, fearing from You,\nوَالْخُشُوعِ وَالْوَفَاءِ وَالتَّسْلِيمِ لَكَ\nWAL KHUSHOO'I WAL WAFAA'I WAT TASLEEMI LAK\nand submitting to You, being loyal to You, complying with You,\nوَالتَّصْدِيقِ بِكِتَابِكَ\nWAT TASDEEQI BIKITAABIK\nbelieving in Your Book,\nوَاتِّبَاعِ سُنَّةِ رَسُولِكَ\nWATTIBAA'I SUNNATI RASOOLIK\nand following Your Prophet’s instructions.\nاَللَّهُمَّ مَا كَانَ فِي قَلْبِي\nALLAAHUMMA MAA KAANA FEE QALBEE\nO Allah, as for whatever I bear in my heart,\nمِنْ شَكٍّ اَوْ رِيبَةٍ\nMIN SHAKKIN AW REEBAH\nincluding suspicion, doubt,\nاَوْ جُحُودٍ اَوْ قُنُوطٍ\nAW JUHOODIN AW QUNOOT\ndenial, despair,\nاَوْ فَرَحٍ اَوْ بَذَخٍ اَوْ بَطَرٍ\nAW FARAHIN AW BADHAKHIN AW BATAR\n(excessive) joy, lavish expenditure or recklessness,\nاَوْ خُيَلاءَ اَوْ رِيَاءٍ اَوْ سُمْعَةٍ\nAW KHUYALAA'A AW RIYAA'IN AW SUM'AH\npride, arrogance, ostentation,\nاَوْ شِقَاقٍ اَوْ نِفَاقٍ\nAW SHIQAAQIN AW NIFAAQ\ndiscord, hypocrisy,\nاَوْ كُفْرٍ اَوْ فُسُوقٍ اَوْ عِصْيَانٍ\nAW KUFRIN AW FUSOOQIN AW I'SYAAN\nunbelief, licentiousness, disobedience,\nاَوْ عَظَمَةٍ اَوْ شَيْءٍ لَا تُحِبُّ\nAW A'ZAMATIN AW SHAY'IN LAA TUHIBB\nconceit, or anything else that You do not like;\nفَاَسْاَلُكَ يَا رَبِّ اَنْ تُبَدِّلَنِي مَكَانَهٗ اِيمَاناً بِوَعْدِكَ\nFA-AS'ALUKA YAA RABBI AN TUBADDILANEE MAKAANAHOO EEMAANAN BIWA'DIK\nI thus beseech You, O my Lord, to substitute all that with belief in Your promise,\nوَوَفَاءً بِعَهْدِكَ\nWA WAFAA'AN BI-A'HDIK\nfulfillment of my covenant to You,\nوَرِضاً بِقَضَائِكَ\nWA RIDAN BIQADAA'IK\nsatisfaction with what You decide for me,\nوَزُهْداً فِي الدُّنْيَا\nWA ZUHDAN FID DUNYAA\nindifference to the worldly pleasures,\nوَرَغْبَةً فِيمَا عِنْدَكَ\nWA RAGHBATAN FEEMAA I'NDAK\ndesire for that which You have,\nوَاَثَرَةً وَطُمَاْنِينَةً\nWA ATHARATAN WA TUMA'NEENAH\naltruism, tranquility,\nوَتَوْبَةً نَصُوحاً\nWA TAWBATAN NASOOHAA\nand sincere repentance.\nاَسْاَلُكَ ذٰلِكَ يَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِينَ\nAS'ALUKA DHAALIKA YAA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN\nI beseech You for all that, O Lord of the worlds!\nاِلٰهِي اَنْتَ مِنْ حِلْمِكَ تُعْصَىٰ فَكَاَنَّكَ لَمْ تُرَ\nILAAHEE ANTA MIN HILMIKA TU'SAA FAKA'ANNAKA LAM TUR\nO my God, because You are so forbearing, You are disobeyed as if You are not present,\nوَمِنْ كَرَمِكَ وَجُودِكَ تُطَاعُ فَكَاَنَّكَ لَمْ تُعْصَ\nWA MIN KARAMIKA WA JOODIKA TUTAA'U FAKA'ANNAKA LAM TU'S\nand because You are so generous and magnanimous, You are obeyed as if You have not been disobeyed at all.\nوَاَنَا وَمَنْ لَمْ يَعْصِكَ سُكَّانُ اَرْضِكَ\nWA ANAA WA MAN LAM YA'SIKA SUKKAANU ARDIK\nBoth those who have not disobeyed You and I are the inhabitants of Your lands;\nفَكُنْ عَلَيْنَا بِالْفَضْلِ جَوَاداً\nFAKUN A'LAYNAA BIL FADLI JAWAADAA\nso, (please) confer magnanimously upon us with Your favors\nوَبِالْخَيْرِ عَوَّاداً\nWA BIL KHAYRI A'WWAADAA\nand always refer to us with Your goodness.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nوَصَلَّىٰ اللَّهُ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ صَلاةً دَائِمَةً\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE SALAATAN DAA'IMAH\nMay Allah bless Muhammad and his Household with endless blessings\nلَا تُحْصَىٰ وَلَا تُعَدُّ\nLAA TUHSAA WA LAA TU'ADD\nthat are innumerable, uncountable,\nوَلَا يَقْدِرُ قَدْرَهَا غَيْرُكَ\nWA LAA YAQDIRU QADRAHAA GHAYRUK\nand none can do it save You.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!",
    "Dua Ya Man Yamliku al-Tadbir\nAfter the Maghrib prayer, raise your hands and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ يَا مَنْ يَمْلِكُ التَّدْبِيْرَ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nALLAAHUMMA YAA MAN YAMLIKUT TADBEERA WA HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nO Allah Who controls the management of all affairs and He has power over all things!\nيَا مَنْ يَعْلَمُ خَآئِنَةَ الْاَعْيُنِ وَمَا تُخْفِيْ الصُّدُوْرِ وَتُجِنُّ الضَّمِيْرُ وَهُوَ اللَّطِيْفُ الْخَبِيْرُ\nYAA MAN YA'LAMU KHAA'INATAL A'YUNI WA MAA TUKHFIS SUDOORI WA TUJINNUD DAMEERU WA HUWAL LATEEFUL KHABEER\nO He Who knows the stealth of looks, that which breasts conceal, and that which selves hide and He is the Knower of subtle, the Aware!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنَا مِمَّنْ نَوٰى فَعَمِلَ، وَلَا تَجْعَلْنَا مِمَّنْ شَقِيَ فَكَسِلَ، وَلَا مِمَّنْ هُوَ عَلٰى غَيْرِ عَمَلٍ يَتَّكِلُ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LNAA MIMMAN NAWAA FA'AMILA WA LAA TAJ'ALNAA MIMMAN SHAQIYA FAKASILA WA LAA MIMMAN HUWA A'LAA GHAYRI A'MALIN YATTAKIL\nO Allah, (please do) include us with those who intend and carried out their intentions, and do not include us with those who are unhappy due to their laziness or with those who depend upon unreal hopes.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَحِّحْ اَبْدَانَنَا مِنَ الْعِلَلِ، وَاَعِنَّا عَلٰى مَا افْتَرَضْتَ عَلَيْنَا مِنَ الْعَمَلِ، حَتّٰى يَنْقَضِيَ عَنَّا شَهْرُكَ هَذَا وَقَدْ اَدَّيْنَا مَفْرُوْضَكَ فِيْهِ عَلَيْنَا\nALLAAHUMMA SAHHIH ABDAANANAA MINAL I'LALI WA A'INNAA A'LAA MAF TARADTA A'LAYNAA MINAL A'MALI HATTAA YANQADIYA A'NNAA SHAHRUKA HAADHAA WA QAD ADDAYNAA MAFROODAKA FEEHI A'LAYNAA\nO Allah, (please do) cure our bodies from ailments and help us carry out the deeds You have made incumbent upon us to do so that when this month, which is Your month, elapses, we shall have carried out all the duties that You have made obligatory upon us to do.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَعِنَّا عَلٰى صِيَامِهٖ، وَوَفِّقْنَا لِقِيَامِهٖ، وَنَشِّطْنَا فِيْهِ لِلصَّلَاةِ، وَلَا تَحْجُبْنَا مِنَ الْقِرَاۤءَةِ، وَسَهِّلْ لَنَا فِيْهِ اِيْتَاۤءَ الزَّكَاةِ\nALLAAHUMMA A'INNAA A'LAA SIYAAMIHEE WA WAFFIQNAA LIQIYAAMIHEE WA NASHSHITNAA FEEHI LIS SALAATI WA LAA TAHJUBNAA MINAL QIRAA'ATI WA SAHHIL LANAA FEEHI EETAA'AZ ZAKAAH\nO Allah, (please do) help us observe fasting in this month, guide us to practice the acts of worship (perfectly), grant us vigor to offer prayers, do not preclude us from reciting (the Holy Qur'an), and make easy for us to give alms.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تُسَلِّطْ عَلَيْنَا وَصَبًا وَلَا تَعَبًا وَلَا سَقَمًا وَلَا عَطَبًا\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TUSALLIT A'LAYNAA WASABAN WA LAA TA'ABAN WA LAA SAQAMAN WA LAA A'TABAA\nO Allah, (please) do not inflict us with fatigue, tiredness, ailment, or injury.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْزُقْنَا الْاِفْطَارَ مِنْ رِزْقِكَ الْحَلَالِ\nALLAAHUMMAR ZUQNAL IFTAARA MIN RIZQIKAL HALAAL\nO Allah, (please do) grant us the food with which we break our fasting from Your sustenance that is legally gotten.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ سَهِّلْ لَنَا فِيْهِ مَا قَسَمْتَهٗ مِنْ رِزْقِكَ، وَيَسِّرْ مَا قَدَّرْتَهٗ مِنْ اَمْرِكَ، وَاجْعَلْهُ حَلَالًا طَيِّبًا نَقِيًّا مِنَ الْاٰثَامِ خَالِصًا مِنَ الْاٰصَارِ وَالْاَجْرَامِ\nALLAAHUMMA SAHHIL LANAA FEEHI MAA QASAMTAHOO MIN RIZQIKA WA YASSIR MAA QADDARTAHOO MIN AMRIKA WAJ'ALHU HALAALAN TAYYIBAN NAQIYYAN MINAL AATHAAMI KHAALISAN MINAL AASAARI WAL AJRAAM\nO Allah, (please do) make easy for us the gaining of Your sustenance that You decide for us, facilitate for us gaining that which You decide for us, and make it pure, empty of sins, and free from offenses and flaws.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تُطْعِمْنَا اِلَّا طَيِّبًا غَيْرَ خَبِيْثٍ وَلَا حَرَامٍ، وَاجْعَلْ رِزْقَكَ لَنَا حَلَالًا لَا يَشُوْبُهٗ دَنَسٌ وَلَا اَسْقَامٌ\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TUT'IMNAA ILLAA TAYYIBAN GHAYRA KHABEETHIN WA LAA HARAAMIN WAJ'AL RIZQAKA LANAA HALAALAN LAA YASHOOBUHOO DANASUN WA LAA ASQAAM\nO Allah, (please) do not feed us except the good that is neither bad nor forbidden. (Please do) let the sustenance that You decide for us be legal, carrying neither filth nor diseases.\nيَا مَنْ عِلْمُهٗ بِالسِّرِّ كَعِلْمِهٖ بِالْاِعْلَانِ، يَا مُتَفَضِّلًا عَلٰى عِبادِهٖ بِالْاِحْسَانِ\nYAA MAN I'LMUHOO BIS SIRRI KA'ILMIHEE BIL I'LAANI YAA MUTAFADDILAN A'LAA I'BAADIHEE BIL IHSAAN\nO He Who knows the secret in the same way as He knows the public! O He Who confers upon His servants with benevolence!\nيَا مَنْ هُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ وَبِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ خَبِيْرٌ\nYAA MAN HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEERUN WA BIKULLI SHAY'IN A'LEEMUN KHABEER\nO He Who has power over all things and has acquaintance with all things!\nاَلْهِمْنَا ذِكْرَكَ وَجَنِّبْنَا عُسْرَكَ، وَاَنِلْنَا يُسْرَكَ، وَاهْدِنَا لِلرَّشَادِ، وَوَفِّقْنَا لِلسَّدَادِ\nALHIMNAA DHIKRAKA WA JANNIBNAA U'SRAKA WA ANILNAA YUSRAKA WAHDINAA LIR RASHAADI WA WAFFIQNAA LIS SADAAD\n(Please do) bestow upon us with (ceaseless) reference to You, keep us away Your difficulty, make us obtain Your ease, guide us to the right path, lead us to righteousness\nوَاعْصِمْنَا مِنَ الْبَلَايَا، وَصُنَّا مِنَ الْاَوْزَارِ وَالْخَطَايَا\nWA'SIMNAA MINAL BALAAYAA WA SUNNAA MINAL AWZAARI WAL KHATAAYAA\nprotect us against misfortunes, and safeguard us against sins and faults.\nيَا مَنْ لَا يَغْفِرُ عَظِيْمَ الذُّنُوْبِ غَيْرُهٗ، وَلَا يَكْشِفُ السُّوٓءَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YAGHFIRU A'ZEEMADH DHUNOOBI GHAYRUHOO WA LAA YAKSHIFUS SOO'A ILLAA HUW\nO He save Whom none forgives the grave sins and none can relieve from hardships!\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ، وَاَكْرَمَ الْاَكْرَمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEENA WA AKRAMAL AKRAMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy and most Generous of all those who show generosity!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ، وَاجْعَلْ صِيَامَنَا مَقْبُوْلًا، وَبِالْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوٰى مَوْصُوْلًا\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AHLI BAYTIHIT TAYYIBEENA WAJ'AL SIYAAMANAA MAQBOOLAN WA BIL BIRRI WAT TAQWAA MAWSOOLAA\n(Please do) send blessings to Muhammad and his Household the pure and decide our fasting to be acceptable and connected to piety and godliness.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ فَاجْعَلْ سَعْيَنَا مَشْكُوْرًا وَقِيَامَنَا مَبْرُوْرًا، وَقُرْاٰنَنَا مَرْفُوْعًا، وَدُعَاۤءَنَا مَسْمُوْعًا\nWA KADHAALIKA FAJ'AL SA'YANAA MASHKOORAN WA QIYAAMANAA MABROORAN WA QUR'AANANAA MARFOO'AN WA DU'AA'ANAA MASMOO'AA\nSimilarly, (please do) decide our efforts to be praiseworthy, our acts of worship admissible, our reciting of the Qur'an raised (to the heavens), and our supplications responded.\nوَاهْدِنَا لِلْحُسْنٰى، وَجَنِّبْنَا الْعُسْرٰى، وَيَسِّرْنَا لِلْيُسْرٰى، وَاَعْلِ لَنَا الدَّرَجَاتِ، وَضَاعِفْ لَنَا الْحَسَنَاتِ\nWAHDINAA LIL HUSNAA WA JANNIBNAL U'SRAA WA YASSIRNAA LIL YUSRAA WA A'LI LANAD DARAJAATI WA DAA'IF LANAL HASANAAT\n(Please do) guide us to the most excellent way, save us from difficulties, facilitate for us the easy end, elevate our ranks, double the rewards for our good deeds\nوَاقْبَلْ مِنَّا الصَّوْمَ وَالصَّلَاةَ، وَاسْمَعْ مِنَّا الدَّعَوَاتِ، وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا الْخَطِيْئَاتِ، وَتَجَاوَزْ عَنَّا السَّيِّئَاتِ\nWAQBAL MINNAS SAWMA WAS SALAATA WASMA' MINNAD DA'AWAATI WAGHFIR LANAL KHATEE'AATI WA TAJAAWAZ A'NNAS SAYYI'AAT\naccept our fasting and prayers, react to our supplications, forgive our sins, overlook our wrongdoings\nوَاجْعَلْنَا مِنَ الْعَامِلِيْنَ الْفَاۤئِزِيْنَ، وَلَا تَجْعَلْنَا مِنَ الْمَغْضُوْبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا الضَّآلِّيْنَ\nWAJ'ALNAA MINAL A'AMILEENAL FAA'IZEENA WA LAA TAJ'ALNAA MINAL MAGHDOOBI A'LAYHIM WA LAD DAALLEEN\nmake us of the successful worshippers, and do not include us with those who earn Your anger nor of those who go astray\nحَتّٰى يَنْقَضِيَ شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ عَنَّا وَقَدْ قَبِلْتَ فِيْهِ صِيَامَنَا وَقِيَامَنَا، وَزَكَّيْتَ فِيْهِ اَعْمَالَنَا، وَغَفَرْتَ فِيْهِ ذُنُوْبَنَا، وَاَجْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ مِنْ كُلِّ خَيْرٍ نَصِيْبَنَا\nHATTAA YANQADIYA SHAHRU RAMADAANA A'NNAA WA QAD QABILTA FEEHI SIYAAMANAA WA QIYAAMANAA WA ZAKKAYTA FEEHI A'MAALANAA WA GHAFARTA FEEHI DHUNOOBANAA WA AJZALTA FEEHI MIN KULLI KHAYRIN NASEEBANAA\nso that when the month of Ramadan elapses, You shall have accepted our fasting and acts of worship, blessed our deeds, forgiven our sins, and doubled our shares from all good things.\nفَاِنَّكَ الْاِلٰهُ الْمُجِيْبُ، وَالرَّبُّ الْقَرِيْبُ، وَاَنْتَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُحِيْطٌ\nFA-INNAKAL ILAAHUL MUJEEBU WAR RABBUL QAREEBU WA ANTA BIKULLI SHAY'IN MUHEET\nVerily, You are the God Who responds, the Lord Who is Nigh, and You encompass all things.",
    "Allahumma Rabba Shahri Ramadan\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ، مُنَزِّلَ الْقُرْاٰنِ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBA SHAHRI RAMADAANA MUNAZZILAL QUR'AAN\nO Allah, the Lord of the month of Ramadan and the Revealer of the Qur'an.\nهٰذَا شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِيْ اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ، وَاَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ اٰيَاتٍ بَيِّنَاتٍ مِنَ الْهُدٰى وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nHAADHAA SHAHRU RAMADAANAL LADHEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR'AANA WA ANZALTA FEEHI AAYAATIN BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nThis is the month of Ramadan in which You revealed the Qur'an and revealed therein chapters of true guidance and distinction (between the right and the wrong).\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْزُقْنَا صِيَامَهٗ، وَاَعِنَّا عَلٰى قِيَامِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMAR ZUQNAA SIYAAMAHOO WA A'INNAA A'LAA QIYAAMIH\nO Allah, make us observe fast in its days and remain awake in its nights to pray.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ سَلِّمْهُ لَنَا وَسَلِّمْنَا فِيْهِ وَتَسَلَّمْهُ مِنَّا فِيْ يُسْرٍ مِنْكَ وَمُعَافَاةٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLIMHU LANAA WA SALLIMNAA FEEHI WA TASALLAMHU MINNAA FEE YUSRIN MINKA WA MU'AAFAAH\nO Allah, let it be peaceful for us, keep us in sound condition for it, and receive it from us with easiness and wellbeing.\nوَاجْعَلْ فِيْمَا تَقْضِيْ وَتُقَدِّرُ مِنَ الْاَمْرِ الْمَحْتُوْمِ وَفِيْمَا تَفْرُقُ مِنَ الْاَمْرِ الْحَكِيْمِ فِيْ لَيْلَةِ الْقَدْرِ مِنَ الْقَضَاۤءِ الَّذِيْ لَا يُرَدُّ وَلَا يُبَدَّلُ\nWAJ'AL FEEMAA TAQDEE WA TUQADDIRU MINAL AMRIL MAHTOOMI WA FEEMAA TAFRUQU MINAL AMRIL HAKEEMI FEE LAYLATIL QADRI MINAL QADAA'IL LADHEE LAA YURADDU WA LAA YUBADDAL\nWhile taking decisions from among Your inevitable decisions and from among that which You decide from the wise affairs at the Destiny Night from the act that is neither rejected nor altered\nاَنْ تَكْتُبَنِيْ مِنْ حُجَّاجِ بَيْتِكَ الْحَرَامِ الْمَبْرُوْرِ حَجُّهُمُ، الْمَشْكُوْرِ سَعْيُهُمُ، الْمَغْفُوْرِ ذُنُوْبُهُمُ، الْمُكَفَّرِ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّئَاتُهُمْ\nAN TAKTUBANEE MIN HUJJAAJI BAYTIKAL HARAAMIL MABROORI HAJJUHUMUL MASHKOORI SA'YUHUMUL MAGHFOORI DHUNOOBUHUMUL MUKAFFARI A'NHUM SAYYI'AATUHUM\n(please) write my name in the list of those pilgrims to Your Sacred House whose pilgrimage receives Your approval, whose efforts are appreciated, whose sins are forgiven, and whose wrongdoings are overlooked.\nوَاجْعَلْ فِيْمَا تَقْضِيْ وَتُقَدِّرُ اَنْ تُطِيْلَ عُمْرِيْ وَتُوَسِّعَ عَلَيَّ مِنَ الرِّزْقِ الْحَلَالِ\nWAJ'AL FEEMAA TAQDEE WA TUQADDIRU AN TUTEELA U'MREE WA TUWASSI'A A'LAYYA MINAR RIZQIL HALAAL\nWhile making decisions and rendering possible things and events, (please) grant me long lifetime and expand my sustenance, making it from legal sources only.",
    "Allahumma Inna Hadha Shahru Ramadan\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ هٰذَا شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA HAADHAA SHAHRU RAMADAAN\nO Allah: This month of Ramadhan,\nاَلَّذي اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ\nALLADHEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR'AAN\nin which You revealed the Qur'an,\nهُدىً لِلنّاسِ وَبَيِّناتٍ مِنَ الْهُدى وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nHUDAA LIN NAASI WA BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nAs guidance for people and clear proofs of true guidance and distinction (between the right and the wrong),\nقَدْ حَضَرَ\nQAD HADAR\nHas commenced.\nيا رَبِّ اَعوذُ بِكَ فِيْهِ مِنَ الشَّيْطانِ الرَّجيمِ\nYAA RABBI A'OODHU BIKA FEEHI MINASH SHAYTAANIR RAJEEM\nO Allah: in this month, I seek Your protection against Satan, the accursed,\nوَمِنْ مَكْرِهٖ وَحِيَلِهٖ\nWA MIN MAKRIHEE WA HIYALIH\nAnd against his tricks and his ruses,\nوَخِداعِهٖ وَحَبائِلِهٖ\nWA KHIDAA'IHEE WA HABAA'ILIH\nAnd his deception and his trickeries,\nوَجُنودِهٖ وَخَيلِهٖ\nWA JUNOODIHEE WA KHAYLIH\nAnd his parties and his riding forces,\nوَرِجْلِهٖ وَوَساوِسِهٖ\nWA RIJLIHEE WA WASAAWISIH\nAnd his on foot forces and his evil inspirations,\nوَمِنَ الضَّلالِ بَعْدَ الْهُدى\nWA MINAD DALAALI BA'DAL HUDAA\nAnd against straying off after being guided,\nوَمِنَ الكُفْرِ بَعْدَ الاِيمانِ\nWA MINAL KUFRI BA'DAL EEMAAN\nAnd against atheism after belief,\nوَمِنَ النِّفاقِ وَالرِّياءِ وَالجِناياتِ\nWA MINAN NIFAAQI WAR RIYAA'I WAL JINAAYAAT\nAnd against hypocrisy and showing off and felonies,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ الوِسْواسِ الخَنّاسِ\nWA MIN SHARRIL WISWAASIL KHANNAAS\nAnd against the evil of the whisperings of the slinking Devil,\nالَّذي يُوَسْوِسُ فِيْ صُدورِ النّاسِ\nALLADHEE YUWASWISU FEE SUDOORIN NAAS\nWho whispers into the hearts of men;\nمِنَ الجِنَّةِ وَالنّاسِ\nMINAL JINNATI WAN NAAS\nFrom among the jinn and the men.\nاللّهُمَّ وَارْزُقْني صِيامَهٗ وَقِيامَهٗ\nALLAAHUMMA WARZUQNEE SIYAAMAHOO WA QIYAAMAH\nO Allah: and confer upon me with the fasting and the doing of acts of worship during this month,\nوَالعَمَلَ فيهِ بِطاعَتِكَ\nWAL A'MALA FEEHI BITAA'ATIK\nAnd with the doing of acts of obedience to You,\nوَطاعَةِ رَسولِكَ وَاُولي الْاَمْرِ\nWA TAA'ATI RASOOLIKA WA ULIL AMR\nAnd to Your Messenger and the Men in Authority,\nعَلَيهِ وَعَلَيهِمُ السَّلامُ\nA'LAYHI WA A'LAYHIMUS SALAAM\nMay peace be upon him and them,\nوَما قَرَّبَ مِنْكَ\nWA MAA QARRABA MINK\nAnd the doing of whatever act that takes me near You,\nوَجَنِّبْني مَعاصِيكَ\nWA JANNIBNEE MA'AASEEK\nAnd (please) take me away from acts of disobedience to You.\nوَارْزُقْني فيهِ التَّوْبَةَ وَالاِنابَةَ وَالاِجابَةَ\nWARZUQNEE FEEHIT TAWBATA WAL INAABATA WAL IJAABAH\nAnd confer upon me in this month with repentance, turning to You, and responding to Your instructions.\nوَاَعِذْني فيهِ مِنَ الغيبَةِ وَالكَسَلِ وَالفَشَلِ\nWA A'IDHNEE FEEHI MINAL GHEEBATI WAL KASALI WAL FASHAL\nAnd protect me in it against backbiting and lethargy and failure.\nوَاسْتَجِبْ لي فيهِ الدُّعاءَ\nWASTAJIB LEE FEEHID DU'AA'\nAnd respond my prayers in it.\nوَاَصِحَّ لي فيهِ جِسمي وَعَقْلي\nWA ASIHHA LEE FEEHI JISMEE WA A'QLEE\nAnd grant me well-being for my body and my intellect.\nوَفَرِّغْني فيهِ لِطاعَتِكَ وَما قَرَّبَ مِنكَ\nWA FARRIGHNEE FEEHI LITAA'ATIKA WA MAA QARRABA MINK\nAnd grant me time to do acts of obedience to You as well as acts that take me near You.\nيا كَريمُ يا جَوادُ\nYAA KAREEMU YAA JAWAAD\nO the All-generous; O the All-magnanimous.\nيا كَريمُ\nYAA KAREEM\nO the All-generous:\nصَلِّ عَلى مُحَمَّدٍ وَعَلى اَهْلِ بَيْتِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA A'LAA AHLI BAYTI MUHAMMAD\n(please) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nعَلَيهِ وَعَلَيهِمُ السَّلامُ\nA'LAYHI WA A'LAYHIMUS SALAAM\nPeace be upon him and them,\nوَكَذالِكَ فَافْعَلْ بِنا\nWA KADHAALIKA FAF'AL BINAA\nAnd do all that to us,\nيا اَرْحَمَ الرّاحِمينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO the most Merciful of all those who show mercy.",
    "Allahumma Hadha Shahru Ramadan al-Mubarak\nOn the first day of Ramazan, or its first night, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ هٰذَا شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الْمُبَارَكُ\nALLAAHUMMA HAADHAA SHAHRU RAMADAANAL MUBAARAK\nO Allah, this blessed month of Ramadan,\nالَّذِيْ اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ\nALLADHEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR'AAN\nin which You sent down the Quran\nوَجَعَلْتَهٗ هُدًى لِلنَّاسِ\nWA JA'ALTAHOO HUDAN LIN NAAS\nand made it a guidance for people\nوَبَيِّنَاتٍ مِنَ الْهُدٰى وَالْفُرْقَانِ قَدْ حَضَرَ\nWA BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAANI QAD HADAR\nand clear proofs of guidance and the Criterion, has come.\nفَسَلِّمْنَا فِيْهِ وَسَلِّمْهُ لَنَا\nFASALLIMNAA FEEHI WA SALLIMHU LANAA\nSo keep us sound in it, keep it sound for us,\nوَتَسَلَّمْهُ مِنَّا فِيْ يُسْرٍ مِنْكَ وَعَافِيَةٍ\nWA TASALLAMHU MINNAA FEE YUSRIN MINKA WA A'AFIYAH\nand accept it from us, with ease and well-being from You.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ اللّٰهُمَّ اَنْ تَغْفِرَ لِيْ فِيْ شَهْرِيْ هٰذَا\nWA AS'ALUKALLAAHUMMA AN TAGHFIRA LEE FEE SHAHREE HAADHAA\nAnd I ask You, O Allah, to forgive me in this month of mine,\nوَتَرْحَمَنِيْ فِيْهِ، وَتُعْتِقَ رَقَبَتِيْ مِنَ النَّارِ\nWA TARHAMANEE FEEHI WA TU'TIQA RAQABATEE MINAN NAAR\nto have mercy on me in it, to free my neck from the Fire,\nوَتُعْطِيَنِيْ فِيْهِ خَيْرَ مَا اَعْطَيْتَ اَحَدًا مِنْ خَلْقِكَ\nWA TU'TIYANEE FEEHI KHAYRA MAA A'TAYTA AHADAN MIN KHALQIK\nand to give me in it the best of what You have given anyone of Your creation\nوَخَيْرَ مَا اَنْتَ مُعْطِيْهِ\nWA KHAYRA MAA ANTA MU'TEEH\nand the best of what You will ever give.\nوَلَا تَجْعَلْهُ اٰخِرَ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ صُمْتُهٗ لَكَ\nWA LAA TAJ'ALHU AAKHIRA SHAHRI RAMADAANA SUMTUHOO LAK\nDo not make it the last month of Ramadan I have fasted for You\nمُنْذُ اَسْكَنْتَنِيْ اَرْضَكَ اِلٰى يَوْمِيْ هٰذَا\nMUNDHU ASKANTANEE ARDAKA ILAA YAWMEE HAADHAA\nsince You settled me on Your earth until this day of mine,\nوَاجْعَلْهُ عَلَيَّ اَتَمَّهٗ نِعْمَةً، وَاَعَمَّهٗ عَافِيَةً\nWAJ'ALHU A'LAYYA ATAMMAHOO NI'MATAN WA A'AMMAHOO A'AFIYAH\nand make it, for me, the most complete [of them] in blessing, the fullest in well-being,\nوَاَوْسَعَهٗ رِزْقًا، وَاَجْزَلَهٗ وَاَهْنَاَهٗ\nWA AWSA'AHOO RIZQAN WA AJZALAHOO WA AHNA'AH\nthe most ample in provision, the most abundant and the most wholesome.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ وَبِوَجْهِكَ الْكَرِيْمِ وَمُلْكِكَ الْعَظِيْمِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA WA BIWAJHIKAL KAREEMI WA MULKIKAL A'ZEEM\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You, in Your noble Face and Your mighty kingdom,\nاَنْ تَغْرُبَ الشَّمْسُ مِنْ يَوْمِيْ هٰذَا\nAN TAGHRUBASH SHAMSU MIN YAWMEE HAADHAA\nlest the sun set on this day of mine,\nاَوْ يَنْقَضِيَ بَقِيَّةُ هٰذَا الْيَوْمِ\nAW YANQADIYA BAQIYYATU HAADHAL YAWM\nor the rest of this day pass,\nاَوْ يَطْلُعَ الْفَجْرُ مِنْ لَيْلَتِيْ هٰذِهٖ\nAW YATLU'AL FAJRU MIN LAYLATEE HAADHIH\nor the dawn break on this night of mine,\nاَوْ يَخْرُجَ هٰذَا الشَّهْرُ\nAW YAKHRUJA HAADHASH SHAHR\nor this month go out\nوَلَكَ قِبَلِيْ مَعَهٗ تَبِعَةٌ اَوْ ذَنْبٌ اَوْ خَطِيْئَةٌ\nWA LAKA QIBALEE MA'AHOO TABI'ATUN AW DHANBUN AW KHATEE'AH\nwhile You still hold against me, as it goes, a liability, a sin or a wrong\nتُرِيْدُ اَنْ تُقَايِسَنِيْ بِذٰلِكَ اَوْ تُؤَاخِذَنِيْ بِهٖ\nTUREEDU AN TUQAAYISANEE BIDHAALIKA AW TU'AAKHIDHANEE BIH\nfor which You would weigh me in the balance or take me to task,\nاَوْ تَقِفَنِيْ بِهٖ مَوْقِفَ خِزْيٍ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nAW TAQIFANEE BIHEE MAWQIFA KHIZYIN FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nor make me stand for it in a place of disgrace in this world and the Hereafter,\nاَوْ تُعَذِّبَنِيْ بِهٖ يَوْمَ اَلْقَاكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nAW TU'ADHDHIBANEE BIHEE YAWMA ALQAAKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nor punish me for it on the day I meet You, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَدْعُوْكَ لِهَمٍّ لَا يُفَرِّجُهٗ غَيْرُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AD'OOKA LIHAMMIN LAA YUFARRIJUHOO GHAYRUK\nO Allah, I call on You for a worry that none but You can lift,\nوَلِرَحْمَةٍ لَا تُنَالُ اِلَّا بِكَ\nWA LIRAHMATIN LAA TUNAALU ILLAA BIK\nfor a mercy that is not attained except through You,\nوَلِكَرْبٍ لَا يَكْشِفُهٗ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nWA LIKARBIN LAA YAKSHIFUHOO ILLAA ANT\nfor a distress that none but You can remove,\nوَلِرَغْبَةٍ لَا تُبْلَغُ اِلَّا بِكَ\nWA LIRAGHBATIN LAA TUBLAGHU ILLAA BIK\nfor a longing that is not reached except through You,\nوَلِحَاجَةٍ لَا تُقْضٰى دُوْنَكَ\nWA LIHAAJATIN LAA TUQDAA DOONAK\nand for a need that is not fulfilled without You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَكَمَا كَانَ مِنْ شَاْنِكَ مَا اَرَدْتَنِيْ بِهٖ مِنْ مَسْاَلَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA FAKAMAA KAANA MIN SHA'NIKA MAA ARADTANEE BIHEE MIN MAS'ALATIK\nO Allah, just as it was Your way to will for me that I ask of You,\nوَرَحِمْتَنِيْ بِهٖ مِنْ ذِكْرِكَ\nWA RAHIMTANEE BIHEE MIN DHIKRIK\nand to show me mercy through remembering You,\nفَلْيَكُنْ مِنْ شَاْنِكَ سَيِّدِي الْاِجَابَةُ لِيْ فِيْمَا دَعَوْتُكَ\nFALYAKUN MIN SHA'NIKA SAYYIDIL IJAABATU LEE FEEMAA DA'AWTUK\nso let it be Your way, my Master, to answer me in what I have called on You for,\nوَالنَّجَاةُ لِيْ فِيْمَا قَدْ فَزِعْتُ اِلَيْكَ مِنْهُ\nWAN NAJAATU LEE FEEMAA QAD FAZI'TU ILAYKA MINH\nand to deliver me from what I have fled in fear to You from.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَافْتَحْ لِيْ مِنْ خَزَائِنِ رَحْمَتِكَ رَحْمَةً\nWAFTAH LEE MIN KHAZAA'INI RAHMATIKA RAHMAH\nand open for me, from the treasuries of Your mercy, a mercy\nلَا تُعَذِّبُنِيْ بَعْدَهَا اَبَدًا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nLAA TU'ADHDHIBUNEE BA'DAHAA ABADAN FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nafter which You will never punish me, in this world or the Hereafter,\nوَارْزُقْنِيْ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ الْوَاسِعِ رِزْقًا حَلَالًا طَيِّبًا\nWARZUQNEE MIN FADLIKAL WAASI'I RIZQAN HALAALAN TAYYIBAA\nand provide me, from Your vast bounty, with lawful and wholesome provision\nلَا تُفْقِرُنِيْ بَعْدَهٗ اِلٰى اَحَدٍ سِوَاكَ اَبَدًا\nLAA TUFQIRUNEE BA'DAHOO ILAA AHADIN SIWAAKA ABADAA\nafter which You will never leave me in need of anyone but You,\nتَزِيْدُنِيْ بِذٰلِكَ لَكَ شُكْرًا وَاِلَيْكَ فَاقَةً وَفَقْرًا\nTAZEEDUNEE BIDHAALIKA LAKA SHUKRAN WA ILAYKA FAAQATAN WA FAQRAA\nincreasing me thereby in gratitude to You, and in need and want of You,\nوَبِكَ عَمَّنْ سِوَاكَ غِنًى وَتَعَفُّفًا\nWA BIKA A'MMAN SIWAAKA GHINAN WA TA'AFFUFAA\nand, through You, in independence and restraint from all besides You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ جَزَاءَ اِحْسَانِكَ الْاِسَاءَةُ مِنِّيْ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA AN TAKOONA JAZAA'A IHSAANIKAL ISAA'ATU MINNEE\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You lest wrongdoing on my part be the return for Your kindness.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ اُصْلِحَ عَمَلِيْ فِيْمَا بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَ النَّاسِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA AN USLIHA A'MALEE FEEMAA BAYNEE WA BAYNAN NAAS\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from setting right my deeds in what is between me and people\nوَاُفْسِدَهٗ فِيْمَا بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَكَ\nWA UFSIDAHOO FEEMAA BAYNEE WA BAYNAK\nand spoiling them in what is between me and You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ تَحُوْلَ سَرِيْرَتِيْ بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA AN TAHOOLA SAREERATEE BAYNEE WA BAYNAK\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You lest my inner self come between me and You,\nاَوْ تَكُوْنَ مُخَالِفَةً لِطَاعَتِكَ\nAW TAKOONA MUKHAALIFATAN LITAA'ATIK\nor be at odds with obedience to You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ يَكُوْنَ شَيْءٌ مِنَ الْاَشْيَاءِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA AN YAKOONA SHAY'UN MINAL ASHYAA'\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You lest anything at all\nاٰثَرَ عِنْدِيْ مِنْ طَاعَتِكَ\nAATHARA I'NDEE MIN TAA'ATIK\nbe dearer to me than obedience to You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ اَعْمَلَ مِنْ طَاعَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA AN A'MALA MIN TAA'ATIK\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from doing any act of obedience to You,\nقَلِيْلًا اَوْ كَثِيْرًا اُرِيْدُ بِهٖ اَحَدًا غَيْرَكَ\nQALEELAN AW KATHEERAN UREEDU BIHEE AHADAN GHAYRAK\nlittle or much, intending by it anyone but You,\nاَوْ اَعْمَلَ عَمَلًا يُخَالِطُهٗ رِيَاءٌ\nAW A'MALA A'MALAN YUKHAALITUHOO RIYAA'\nor doing a deed mixed with showing off.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ هَوًى يُرْدِيْ مَنْ يَرْكَبُهٗ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA MIN HAWAN YURDEE MAN YARKABUH\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from a desire that ruins whoever rides it.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ اَجْعَلَ شَيْئًا مِنْ شُكْرِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA AN AJ'ALA SHAY'AN MIN SHUKREE\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from giving any of my thanks\nفِيْمَا اَنْعَمْتَ بِهٖ عَلَيَّ لِغَيْرِكَ اَطْلُبُ بِهٖ رِضَا خَلْقِكَ\nFEEMAA AN'AMTA BIHEE A'LAYYA LIGHAYRIKA ATLUBU BIHEE RIDAA KHALQIK\nfor what You have bestowed on me to other than You, seeking by it the pleasure of Your creatures.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ اَتَعَدّٰى حَدًّا مِنْ حُدُوْدِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA AN ATA'ADDAA HADDAN MIN HUDOODIK\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from overstepping any of Your limits,\nاَتَزَيَّنُ بِذٰلِكَ لِلنَّاسِ وَاَرْكَنُ بِهٖ اِلَى الدُّنْيَا\nATAZAYYANU BIDHAALIKA LIN NAASI WA ARKANU BIHEE ILAD DUNYAA\nadorning myself by it before people and leaning by it towards this world.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِعَفْوِكَ مِنْ عُقُوْبَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BI-A'FWIKA MIN U'QOOBATIK\nO Allah, I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment,\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِرِضَاكَ مِنْ سَخَطِكَ\nWA A'OODHU BIRIDAAKA MIN SAKHATIK\nI seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger,\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِطَاعَتِكَ مِنْ مَعْصِيَتِكَ، وَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْكَ\nWA A'OODHU BITAA'ATIKA MIN MA'SIYATIKA WA A'OODHU BIKA MINK\nI seek refuge in obeying You from disobeying You, and I seek refuge in You from You.\nجَلَّ ثَنَاءُ وَجْهِكَ، لَا اُحْصِي الثَّنَاءَ عَلَيْكَ وَلَوْ حَرَصْتُ\nJALLA THANAA'U WAJHIKA LAA UHSITH THANAA'A A'LAYKA WA LAW HARAST\nMajestic is the praise of Your Face! I cannot count Your praise, however hard I try,\nوَاَنْتَ كَمَا اَثْنَيْتَ عَلٰى نَفْسِكَ، سُبْحَانَكَ وَبِحَمْدِكَ\nWA ANTA KAMAA ATHNAYTA A'LAA NAFSIKA SUBHAANAKA WA BIHAMDIK\nand You are as You have praised Yourself. Glory be to You, and with Your praise.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASTAGHFIRUKA WA ATOOBU ILAYK\nO Allah, I ask Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance\nمِنْ مَظَالِمَ كَثِيْرَةٍ لِعِبَادِكَ عِنْدِيْ\nMIN MAZAALIMA KATHEERATIN LI-I'BAADIKA I'NDEE\nfor the many wrongs I owe Your servants.\nفَاَيُّمَا عَبْدٍ مِنْ عِبَادِكَ اَوْ اَمَةٍ مِنْ اِمَائِكَ\nFA-AYYUMAA A'BDIN MIN I'BAADIKA AW AMATIN MIN IMAA'IK\nSo whichever of Your servants, man or woman,\nكَانَتْ لَهٗ قِبَلِيْ مَظْلِمَةٌ ظَلَمْتُهٗ اِيَّاهَا\nKAANAT LAHOO QIBALEE MAZLIMATUN ZALAMTUHOO IYYAAHAA\nhas a claim against me for a wrong I did them,\nفِيْ مَالِهٖ اَوْ بَدَنِهٖ اَوْ عِرْضِهٖ\nFEE MAALIHEE AW BADANIHEE AW I'RDIH\nin their property, their body or their honour,\nلَا اَسْتَطِيْعُ اَدَاءَ ذٰلِكَ اِلَيْهِ وَلَا اَتَحَلَّلُهَا مِنْهُ\nLAA ASTATEE'U ADAA'A DHAALIKA ILAYHI WA LAA ATAHALLALUHAA MINH\nwhich I cannot repay to them, nor seek their release from,\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nthen bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاَرْضِهٖ اَنْتَ عَنِّيْ بِمَا شِئْتَ وَكَيْفَ شِئْتَ وَهَبْهَا لِيْ\nWA ARDIHEE ANTA A'NNEE BIMAA SHI'TA WA KAYFA SHI'TA WA HABHAA LEE\nand satisfy them Yourself on my behalf, with whatever You will and however You will, and make it a gift to me.\nوَمَا تَصْنَعُ يَا سَيِّدِيْ بِعَذَابِيْ\nWA MAA TASNA'U YAA SAYYIDEE BI-A'DHAABEE\nAnd what would You do with my punishment, my Master,\nوَقَدْ وَسِعَتْ رَحْمَتُكَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ\nWA QAD WASI'AT RAHMATUKA KULLA SHAY'\nwhen Your mercy encompasses all things?\nوَمَا عَلَيْكَ يَا رَبِّ اَنْ تُكْرِمَنِيْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ\nWA MAA A'LAYKA YAA RABBI AN TUKRIMANEE BIRAHMATIK\nAnd what would it cost You, my Lord, to honour me with Your mercy\nوَلَا تُهِيْنَنِيْ بِعَذَابِكَ\nWA LAA TUHEENANEE BI-A'DHAABIK\nand not disgrace me with Your punishment?\nوَلَا يَنْقُصُكَ يَا رَبِّ اَنْ تَفْعَلَ بِيْ مَا سَاَلْتُكَ\nWA LAA YANQUSUKA YAA RABBI AN TAF'ALA BEE MAA SA'ALTUK\nNor does it lessen You, my Lord, to do for me what I have asked of You,\nوَاَنْتَ وَاجِدٌ لِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nWA ANTA WAAJIDUN LIKULLI SHAY'\nwhen You have the means for all things.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASTAGHFIRUKA WA ATOOBU ILAYK\nO Allah, I ask Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance\nمِنْ كُلِّ ذَنْبٍ تُبْتُ اِلَيْكَ مِنْهُ ثُمَّ عُدْتُ فِيْهِ\nMIN KULLI DHANBIN TUBTU ILAYKA MINHU THUMMA U'DTU FEEH\nfor every sin I repented of to You and then went back to,\nوَمِمَّا ضَيَّعْتُ مِنْ فَرَائِضِكَ وَاَدَاءِ حَقِّكَ\nWA MIMMAA DAYYA'TU MIN FARAA'IDIKA WA ADAA'I HAQQIK\nand for what I neglected of Your obligations and of fulfilling Your due:\nمِنَ الصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ وَالصِّيَامِ وَالْجِهَادِ وَالْحَجِّ وَالْعُمْرَةِ\nMINAS SALAATI WAZ ZAKAATI WAS SIYAAMI WAL JIHAADI WAL HAJJI WAL U'MRAH\nprayer, zakat, fasting, jihad, the Hajj and the Umrah,\nوَاِسْبَاغِ الْوُضُوْءِ وَالْغُسْلِ مِنَ الْجَنَابَةِ\nWA ISBAAGHIL WUDOO'I WAL GHUSLI MINAL JANAABAH\ndoing wudu thoroughly and the ghusl for major impurity,\nوَقِيَامِ اللَّيْلِ وَكَثْرَةِ الذِّكْرِ وَكَفَّارَةِ الْيَمِيْنِ\nWA QIYAAMIL LAYLI WA KATHRATIDH DHIKRI WA KAFFAARATIL YAMEEN\nstanding in prayer at night, remembering You often, atoning for broken oaths,\nوَالْاِسْتِرْجَاعِ فِي الْمَعْصِيَةِ\nWAL ISTIRJAA'I FIL MA'SIYAH\nturning back [to You] upon a sin,\nوَالصُّدُوْدِ مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَصَّرْتُ فِيْهِ مِنْ فَرِيْضَةٍ اَوْ سُنَّةٍ\nWAS SUDOODI MIN KULLI SHAY'IN QASSARTU FEEHI MIN FAREEDATIN AW SUNNAH\nand turning away from anything I fell short in, obligatory or recommended.\nفَاِنِّيْ اَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْكَ مِنْهُ\nFA-INNEE ASTAGHFIRUKA WA ATOOBU ILAYKA MINH\nSo I ask Your forgiveness for it and turn to You in repentance,\nوَمِمَّا رَكِبْتُ مِنَ الْكَبَائِرِ، وَاَتَيْتُ مِنَ الْمَعَاصِيْ\nWA MIMMAA RAKIBTU MINAL KABAA'IRI WA ATAYTU MINAL MA'AASEE\nand for the grave sins I have committed, the acts of disobedience I have done,\nوَعَمِلْتُ مِنَ الذُّنُوْبِ، وَاجْتَرَحْتُ مِنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ\nWA A'MILTU MINADH DHUNOOBI WAJTARAHTU MINAS SAYYI'AAT\nthe sins I have worked, the evil deeds I have perpetrated,\nوَاَصَبْتُ مِنَ الشَّهَوَاتِ، وَبَاشَرْتُ مِنَ الْخَطَايَا\nWA ASABTU MINASH SHAHAWAATI WA BAASHARTU MINAL KHATAAYAA\nthe lusts I have indulged and the wrongs I have engaged in,\nمِمَّا عَمِلْتُهٗ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ عَمْدًا اَوْ خَطَاً سِرًّا اَوْ عَلَانِيَةً\nMIMMAA A'MILTUHOO MIN DHAALIKA A'MDAN AW KHATA'AN SIRRAN AW A'LAANIYAH\nwhatever of that I did on purpose or by mistake, in secret or in the open.\nفَاِنِّيْ اَتُوْبُ اِلَيْكَ مِنْهُ، وَمِنْ سَفْكِ الدَّمِ\nFA-INNEE ATOOBU ILAYKA MINHU WA MIN SAFKID DAM\nSo I turn to You in repentance from that, and from shedding blood,\nوَعُقُوْقِ الْوَالِدَيْنِ، وَقَطِيْعَةِ الرَّحِمِ، وَالْفِرَارِ مِنَ الزَّحْفِ\nWA U'QOOQIL WAALIDAYNI WA QATEE'ATIR RAHIMI WAL FIRAARI MINAZ ZAHF\ndisobeying parents, severing the ties of kinship, fleeing from the battlefield,\nوَقَذْفِ الْمُحْصَنَاتِ، وَاَكْلِ اَمْوَالِ الْيَتَامٰى ظُلْمًا\nWA QADHFIL MUHSANAATI WA AKLI AMWAALIL YATAAMAA ZULMAA\nslandering chaste women, devouring the property of orphans unjustly,\nوَشَهَادَةِ الزُّوْرِ، وَكِتْمَانِ الشَّهَادَةِ\nWA SHAHAADATIZ ZOORI WA KITMAANISH SHAHAADAH\nfalse testimony, concealing testimony,\nوَاَنْ اَشْتَرِيَ بِعَهْدِكَ فِيْ نَفْسِيْ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا\nWA AN ASHTARIYA BI-A'HDIKA FEE NAFSEE THAMANAN QALEELAA\nselling, in my own case, Your covenant for a paltry price,\nوَاَكْلِ الرِّبَا وَالْغُلُوْلِ، وَالسُّحْتِ وَالسِّحْرِ\nWA AKLIR RIBAA WAL GHULOOLI WAS SUHTI WAS SIHR\nconsuming usury, embezzlement and unlawful gain, sorcery,\nوَالْكِتْمَانِ وَالطِّيَرَةِ، وَالشِّرْكِ وَالرِّيَاۤءِ وَالسَّرِقَةِ\nWAL KITMAANI WAT TIYARATI WASH SHIRKI WAR RIYAA'I WAS SARIQAH\nconcealment [of the truth], taking evil omens, polytheism, showing off, theft,\nوَشُرْبِ الْخَمْرِ، وَنَقْصِ الْمِكْيَالِ، وَبَخْسِ الْمِيْزَانِ\nWA SHURBIL KHAMRI WA NAQSIL MIKYAALI WA BAKHSIL MEEZAAN\ndrinking wine, giving short measure, cheating in the scales,\nوَالشِّقَاقِ وَالنِّفَاقِ، وَنَقْضِ الْعَهْدِ\nWASH SHIQAAQI WAN NIFAAQI WA NAQDIL A'HD\ndiscord and hypocrisy, breaking pledges,\nوَالْفِرْيَةِ وَالْخِيَانَةِ وَالْغَدْرِ، وَاِخْفَارِ الذِّمَّةِ وَالْحَلْفِ\nWAL FIRYATI WAL KHIYAANATI WAL GHADRI WA IKHFAARIDH DHIMMATI WAL HALF\nfabrication, betraying trust, treachery, breaking a pledge of protection, swearing [oaths],\nوَالْغِيْبَةِ وَالنَّمِيْمَةِ وَالْبُهْتَانِ\nWAL GHEEBATI WAN NAMEEMATI WAL BUHTAAN\nbackbiting, talebearing and slander,\nوَالْهَمْزِ وَاللَّمْزِ وَالتَّنَابُزِ بِالْاَلْقَابِ\nWAL HAMZI WAL LAMZI WAT TANAABUZI BIL ALQAAB\ndefaming, faultfinding, insulting one another with nicknames,\nوَاَذَى الْجَارِ، وَدُخُوْلِ بَيْتٍ بِغَيْرِ اِذْنٍ\nWA ADHAL JAARI WA DUKHOOLI BAYTIN BIGHAYRI IDHN\nharming the neighbor, entering a house without permission,\nوَالْفَخْرِ وَالْكِبْرِ، وَالْاِشْرَاكِ وَالْاِصْرَارِ وَالْاِسْتِكْبَارِ\nWAL FAKHRI WAL KIBRI WAL ISHRAAKI WAL ISRAARI WAL ISTIKBAAR\nboasting and pride, associating partners [with You], persisting [in sin], arrogance,\nوَالْمَشْيِ فِي الْاَرْضِ مَرَحًا، وَالْجَوْرِ فِي الْحُكْمِ\nWAL MASHYI FIL ARDI MARAHAN WAL JAWRI FIL HUKM\nwalking on the earth exultantly, injustice in judgment,\nوَالْاِعْتِدَاۤءِ فِي الْغَضَبِ، وَرُكُوْبِ الْحَمِيَّةِ\nWAL I'TIDAA'I FIL GHADABI WA RUKOOBIL HAMIYYAH\ntransgressing in anger, giving way to bigoted zeal,\nوَتَعَضُّدِ الظَّالِمِ، وَعَوْنٍ عَلَى الْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ\nWA TA'ADDUDIZ ZAALIMI WA A'WNIN A'LAL ITHMI WAL U'DWAAN\nbacking the oppressor, helping in sin and aggression,\nوَقِلَّةِ الْعَدَدِ فِي الْاَهْلِ وَالْمَالِ وَالْوَلَدِ\nWA QILLATIL A'DADI FIL AHLI WAL MAALI WAL WALAD\nfewness in number among family, wealth and children,\nوَرُكُوْبِ الظَّنِّ، وَاتِّبَاعِ الْهَوٰى، وَالْعَمَلِ بِالشَّهْوَةِ\nWA RUKOOBIZ ZANNI WATTIBAA'IL HAWAA WAL A'MALI BISH SHAHWAH\nacting on suspicion, following [vain] desire, acting out of lust,\nوَالْاَمْرِ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَالنَّهْيِ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ\nWAL AMRI BIL MA'ROOFI WAN NAHYI A'NIL MUNKAR\n[failing in] enjoining good and forbidding evil,\nوَفَسَادٍ فِي الْاَرْضِ، وَجُحُوْدِ الْحَقِّ\nWA FASAADIN FIL ARDI WA JUHOODIL HAQQ\ncorruption in the land, denying the truth,\nوَالْاِدْلَاۤءِ اِلَى الْحُكَّامِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ\nWAL IDLAA'I ILAL HUKKAAMI BIGHAYRIL HAQQ\ntaking [disputes] to rulers without right,\nوَالْمَكْرِ وَالْخَدِيْعَةِ وَالْبُخْلِ، وَقَوْلٍ فِيْمَا لَا اَعْلَمُ\nWAL MAKRI WAL KHADEE'ATI WAL BUKHLI WA QAWLIN FEEMAA LAA A'LAM\nscheming, deceit and miserliness, speaking about what I do not know,\nوَاَكْلِ الْمَيْتَةِ وَالدَّمِ وَلَحْمِ الْخِنْزِيْرِ، وَمَا اُهِلَّ لِغَيْرِ اللّٰهِ بِهٖ\nWA AKLIL MAYTATI WAD DAMI WA LAHMIL KHINZEERI WA MAA UHILLA LIGHAYRILLAAHI BIH\neating carrion, blood, the flesh of swine, and what has been offered to other than Allah,\nوَالْحَسَدِ وَالْبَغْيِ، وَالدُّعَاۤءِ اِلَى الْفَاحِشَةِ\nWAL HASADI WAL BAGHYI WAD DU'AA'I ILAL FAAHISHAH\nenvy and oppression, inviting to indecency,\nوَالتَّمَنِّيْ بِمَا فَضَّلَ اللّٰهُ، وَالْاِعْجَابِ بِالنَّفْسِ\nWAT TAMANNEE BIMAA FADDALALLAAHU WAL I'JAABI BIN NAFS\ncoveting that with which Allah has favored [others], self-admiration,\nوَالْمَنِّ بِالْعَطِيَّةِ، وَالْاِرْتِكَابِ اِلَى الظُّلْمِ\nWAL MANNI BIL A'TIYYATI WAL IRTIKAABI ILAZ ZULM\nreminding [others] of a gift given, resorting to wrongdoing,\nوَجُحُوْدِ الْقُرْاٰنِ، وَقَهْرِ الْيَتِيْمِ، وَانْتِهَارِ السَّاۤئِلِ\nWA JUHOODIL QUR'AANI WA QAHRIL YATEEMI WANTIHAARIS SAA'IL\ndenying the Qur'an, oppressing the orphan, rebuffing the beggar,\nوَالْحِنْثِ فِي الْاَيْمَانِ، وَكُلِّ يَمِيْنٍ كَاذِبَةٍ فَاجِرَةٍ\nWAL HINTHI FIL AYMAANI WA KULLI YAMEENIN KAADHIBATIN FAAJIRAH\nbreaking oaths, every lying, wicked oath,\nوَظُلْمِ اَحَدٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ فِيْ اَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَشْعَارِهِمْ وَاَعْرَاضِهِمْ وَاَبْشَارِهِمْ\nWA ZULMI AHADIN MIN KHALQIKA FEE AMWAALIHIM WA ASH'AARIHIM WA A'RAADIHIM WA ABSHAARIHIM\nand wronging any of Your creatures in their property, their hair, their honor or their skin;\nوَمَا رَاٰهُ بَصَرِيْ، وَسَمِعَهٗ سَمْعِيْ، وَنَطَقَ بِهٖ لِسَانِيْ\nWA MAA RA'AAHU BASAREE WA SAMI'AHOO SAM'EE WA NATAQA BIHEE LISAANEE\nand from what my eyes have seen, my ears have heard and my tongue has spoken,\nوَبَسَطْتُ اِلَيْهِ يَدِيْ، وَنَقَلْتُ قَدَمِيْ\nWA BASATTU ILAYHI YADEE WA NAQALTU QADAMEE\nwhat I have stretched out my hand to and moved my feet towards,\nوَبَاشَرَهٗ جِلْدِيْ، وَحَدَّثْتُ بِهٖ نَفْسِيْ\nWA BAASHARAHOO JILDEE WA HADDATHTU BIHEE NAFSEE\nwhat my skin has touched and what I have spoken of to myself,\nمِمَّا هُوَ لَكَ مَعْصِيَةٌ، وَكُلِّ يَمِيْنِ زُوْرٍ\nMIMMAA HUWA LAKA MA'SIYATUN WA KULLI YAMEENI ZOOR\nof whatever is disobedience to You, and every false oath;\nوَمِنْ كُلِّ فَاحِشَةٍ وَذَنْبٍ وَخَطِيْئَةٍ عَمِلْتُهَا\nWA MIN KULLI FAAHISHATIN WA DHANBIN WA KHATEE'ATIN A'MILTUHAA\nand from every indecency, sin and wrong that I have done\nفِيْ سَوَادِ اللَّيْلِ وَبَيَاضِ النَّهَارِ، فِيْ مَلَاٍ اَوْ خَلَاۤءٍ\nFEE SAWAADIL LAYLI WA BAYAADIN NAHAARI FEE MALAAN AW KHALAA'\nin the darkness of night and the brightness of day, in company or alone,\nمِمَّا عَلِمْتُهٗ اَوْ لَمْ اَعْلَمْهُ، ذَكَرْتُهٗ اَوْ لَمْ اَذْكُرْهُ، سَمِعْتُهٗ اَوْ لَمْ اَسْمَعْهُ\nMIMMAA A'LIMTUHOO AW LAM A'LAMHU DHAKARTUHOO AW LAM ADHKURHU SAMI'TUHOO AW LAM ASMA'H\nwhether I knew of it or not, remember it or not, heard of it or not,\nعَصَيْتُكَ فِيْهِ رَبِّيْ طَرْفَةَ عَيْنٍ\nA'SAYTUKA FEEHI RABBEE TARFATA A'YN\nin which I disobeyed You, my Lord, for the blink of an eye,\nوَفِيْمَا سِوَاهَا مِنْ حِلٍّ اَوْ حَرَامٍ تَعَدَّيْتُ فِيْهِ اَوْ قَصَّرْتُ عَنْهُ\nWA FEEMAA SIWAAHAA MIN HILLIN AW HARAAMIN TA'ADDAYTU FEEHI AW QASSARTU A'NH\nand in anything besides, lawful or unlawful, in which I overstepped or fell short,\nمُنْذُ يَوْمِ خَلَقْتَنِيْ اِلٰى اَنْ جَلَسْتُ مَجْلِسِيْ هٰذَا\nMUNDHU YAWMI KHALAQTANEE ILAA AN JALASTU MAJLISEE HAADHAA\nfrom the day You created me until I sat in this place of mine;\nفَاِنِّيْ اَتُوْبُ اِلَيْكَ مِنْهُ، وَاَنْتَ يَا كَرِيْمُ تَوَّابٌ رَحِيْمٌ\nFA-INNEE ATOOBU ILAYKA MINHU WA ANTA YAA KAREEMU TAWWAABUN RAHEEM\nfor I turn to You in repentance from it, and You, O Generous One, are Ever-Relenting, Merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ يَا ذَا الْمَنِّ وَالْفَضْلِ، وَالْمَحَامِدِ الَّتِيْ لَا تُحْصٰى\nALLAAHUMMA YAA DHAL MANNI WAL FADLI WAL MAHAAMIDIL LATEE LAA TUHSAA\nO Allah, O Possessor of favor and bounty, and of praises beyond counting,\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ، وَاقْبَلْ تَوْبَتِيْ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WAQBAL TAWBATEE\nbless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and accept my repentance.\nلَا تَرُدَّهَا لِكَثْرَةِ ذُنُوْبِيْ، وَمَا اَسْرَفْتُ عَلٰى نَفْسِيْ\nLAA TARUDDAHAA LIKATHRATI DHUNOOBEE WA MAA ASRAFTU A'LAA NAFSEE\nDo not reject it because of my many sins and the excesses I have committed against myself,\nحَتّٰى لَا اَرْجِعَ فِيْ ذَنْبٍ تُبْتُ اِلَيْكَ مِنْهُ\nHATTAA LAA ARJI'A FEE DHANBIN TUBTU ILAYKA MINH\nso that I do not go back to any sin from which I have repented to You.\nفَاجْعَلْهَا يَا عَزِيْزُ تَوْبَةً نَصُوْحًا صَادِقَةً مَبْرُوْرَةً\nFAJ'ALHAA YAA A'ZEEZU TAWBATAN NASOOHAN SAADIQATAN MABROORAH\nSo make it, O Mighty One, a sincere repentance, truthful and righteous,\nلَدَيْكَ مَقْبُوْلَةً مَرْفُوْعَةً عِنْدَكَ\nLADAYKA MAQBOOLATAN MARFOO'ATAN I'NDAK\naccepted by You, raised up to You,\nفِيْ خَزَاۤئِنِكَ الَّتِيْ ذَخَرْتَهَا لِاَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ\nFEE KHAZAA'INIKAL LATEE DHAKHARTAHAA LI-AWLIYAA'IK\n[kept] in Your treasuries that You have stored up for Your friends\nحِيْنَ قَبِلْتَهَا مِنْهُمْ وَرَضِيْتَ بِهَا عَنْهُمْ\nHEENA QABILTAHAA MINHUM WA RADEETA BIHAA A'NHUM\nwhen You accepted it from them and were pleased with them for it.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ هٰذِهِ النَّفْسَ نَفْسُ عَبْدِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA HAADHIHIN NAFSA NAFSU A'BDIK\nO Allah, this soul is the soul of Your servant,\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA AS'ALUKA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nand I ask You to bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاَنْ تُحَصِّنَهَا مِنَ الذُّنُوْبِ، وَتَمْنَعَهَا مِنَ الْخَطَايَا\nWA AN TUHASSINAHAA MINADH DHUNOOBI WA TAMNA'AHAA MINAL KHATAAYAA\nto fortify it against sins, to shield it from wrongs,\nوَتُحْرِزَهَا مِنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ، وَتَجْعَلَهَا فِيْ حِصْنٍ حَصِيْنٍ مَنِيْعٍ\nWA TUHRIZAHAA MINAS SAYYI'AATI WA TAJ'ALAHAA FEE HISNIN HASEENIN MANEE'\nto guard it from evil deeds, and to place it in a strong, impregnable fortress\nلَا يَصِلُ اِلَيْهَا ذَنْبٌ وَلَا خَطِيْئَةٌ، وَلَا يُفْسِدُهَا عَيْبٌ وَلَا مَعْصِيَةٌ\nLAA YASILU ILAYHAA DHANBUN WA LAA KHATEE'ATUN WA LAA YUFSIDUHAA A'YBUN WA LAA MA'SIYAH\nthat no sin or wrong can reach and no fault or disobedience can corrupt,\nحَتّٰى اَلْقَاكَ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَاَنْتَ عَنِّيْ رَاضٍ وَاَنَا مَسْرُوْرٌ\nHATTAA ALQAAKA YAWMAL QIYAAMATI WA ANTA A'NNEE RAADIN WA ANAA MASROOR\nuntil I meet You on the Day of Resurrection, You pleased with me and I joyful,\nتَغْبِطُنِيْ مَلَاۤئِكَتُكَ وَاَنْبِيَاۤؤُكَ وَجَمِيْعُ خَلْقِكَ\nTAGHBITUNEE MALAA'IKATUKA WA ANBIYAA'UKA WA JAMEE'U KHALQIK\nwith Your angels, Your prophets and all Your creatures envying my lot,\nوَقَدْ قَبِلْتَنِيْ وَجَعَلْتَنِيْ طَاۤئِعًا طَاهِرًا زَاكِيًا عِنْدَكَ مِنَ الصَّادِقِيْنَ\nWA QAD QABILTANEE WA JA'ALTANEE TAA'I'AN TAAHIRAN ZAAKIYAN I'NDAKA MINAS SAADIQEEN\nfor You will have accepted me and made me obedient, pure and purified, one of the truthful in Your sight.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعْتَرِفُ لَكَ بِذُنُوْبِيْ، فَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'TARIFU LAKA BIDHUNOOBEE FASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, I confess my sins to You, so bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاجْعَلْهَا ذُنُوْبًا لَا تُظْهِرُهَا لِاَحَدٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ\nWAJ'ALHAA DHUNOOBAN LAA TUZHIRUHAA LI-AHADIN MIN KHALQIK\nand make them sins that You do not reveal to any of Your creatures,\nوَيَا غَفَّارَ الذُّنُوْبِ، يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nWA YAA GHAFFAARADH DHUNOOBI YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO Forgiver of sins, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nسُبْحَانَكَ اللّٰهُمَّ وَبِحَمْدِكَ، عَمِلْتُ سُوْۤءًا وَظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِيْ\nSUBHAANAKALLAAHUMMA WA BIHAMDIKA A'MILTU SOO'AN WA ZALAMTU NAFSEE\nGlory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I have done evil and wronged myself,\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاغْفِرْ لِيْ، اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WAGHFIR LEE INNAKA ANTAL GHAFOORUR RAHEEM\nso bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad and forgive me; surely You are the All-Forgiving, the Merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنْ كَانَ مِنْ عَطَاۤئِكَ وَمَنِّكَ وَفَضْلِكَ، وَفِيْ عِلْمِكَ وَقَضَاۤئِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA IN KAANA MIN A'TAA'IKA WA MANNIKA WA FADLIKA WA FEE I'LMIKA WA QADAA'IK\nO Allah, if it is of Your giving, Your favor and Your bounty, and in Your knowledge and Your decree,\nاَنْ تَرْزُقَنِيَ التَّوْبَةَ، فَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهٖ\nAN TARZUQANIYAT TAWBATA FASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nthat You grant me repentance, then bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاعْصِمْنِيْ بَقِيَّةَ عُمْرِيْ، وَاَحْسِنْ مَعُوْنَتِيْ\nWA'SIMNEE BAQIYYATA U'MREE WA AHSIN MA'OONATEE\nkeep me from sin for the rest of my life, and help me well\nفِي الْجِدِّ وَالْاِجْتِهَادِ، وَالْمُسَارَعَةِ اِلٰى مَا تُحِبُّ وَتَرْضٰى\nFIL JIDDI WAL IJTIHAADI WAL MUSAARA'ATI ILAA MAA TUHIBBU WA TARDAA\nin diligence and striving, and in hastening to what You love and are pleased with,\nوَالنَّشَاطِ وَالْفَرَحِ وَالصِّحَّةِ، حَتّٰى اَبْلُغَ فِيْ عِبَادَتِكَ وَطَاعَتِكَ\nWAN NASHAATI WAL FARAHI WAS SIHHATI HATTAA ABLUGHA FEE I'BAADATIKA WA TAA'ATIK\nand with vigor, joy and health, so that, through worshipping and obeying You\nالَّتِيْ يَحِقُّ لَكَ عَلَيَّ رِضَاكَ\nALLATEE YAHIQQU LAKA A'LAYYA RIDAAK\nas is Your due from me, I may attain Your good pleasure.\nوَاَنْ تَرْزُقَنِيْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ مَا اُقِيْمُ بِهٖ حُدُوْدَ دِيْنِكَ\nWA AN TARZUQANEE BIRAHMATIKA MAA UQEEMU BIHEE HUDOODA DEENIK\nAnd [I ask] that You grant me, by Your mercy, the means to uphold the bounds of Your religion,\nوَحَتّٰى اَعْمَلَ فِيْ ذٰلِكَ بِسُنَنِ نَبِيِّكَ، صَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nWA HATTAA A'MALA FEE DHAALIKA BISUNANI NABIYYIKA SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nand that I may act therein by the practices of Your Prophet, Your blessings be upon him and his Household;\nوَافْعَلْ ذٰلِكَ بِجَمِيْعِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ فِيْ مَشَارِقِ الْاَرْضِ وَمَغَارِبِهَا\nWAF'AL DHAALIKA BIJAMEE'IL MU'MINEENA WAL MU'MINAATI FEE MASHAARIQIL ARDI WA MAGHAARIBIHAA\nand do the same for all believing men and women, in the east of the earth and its west.\nThen recite three times:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ تَشْكُرُ الْيَسِيْرَ وَتَغْفِرُ الْكَثِيْرَ، وَاَنْتَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA TASHKURUL YASEERA WA TAGHFIRUL KATHEERA WA ANTAL GHAFOORUR RAHEEM\nO Allah, You reward the little and forgive the much, and You are the All-Forgiving, the Merciful.",
    "Duas of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)\nAt the beginning of Ramazan, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّهٗ قَدْ دَخَلَ شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAHOO QAD DAKHALA SHAHRU RAMADAAN\nO Allah, the month of Ramadan has begun.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ، الَّذِيْ اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ، وَجَعَلْتَهٗ بَيِّنَاتٍ مِنَ الْهُدٰى وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBA SHAHRI RAMADAANAL LADHEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR'AANA WA JA'ALTAHOO BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nO Allah, the Lord of the month of Ramadan in which You have revealed the Qur'an making it guidance to people and clear proofs of the guidance and the distinction.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَبَارِكْ لَنَا فِيْ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ، وَاَعِنَّا عَلٰى صِيَامِهٖ وَصَلَوَاتِهٖ وَتَقَبَّلْهُ مِنَّا\nALLAAHUMMA FABAARIK LANAA FEE SHAHRI RAMADAANA WA A'INNAA A'LAA SIYAAMIHEE WA SALAWAATIHEE WA TAQABBALHU MINNAA\nSo, O Allah, please bless us in the month of Ramadan, help us observe fasting and offer prayers in it, and accept from us.\nOn the first night of Ramazan, recite:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ اَكْرَمَنَا بِكَ اَيُّهَا الشَّهْرُ الْمُبَارَكُ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE AKRAMANAA BIKA AYYUHASH SHAHRUL MUBAARAK\nAll praise be to Allah Who has honored us with you, O blessed month.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَقَوِّنَا عَلٰى صِيَامِنَا وَقِيَامِنَا، وَثَبِّتْ اَقْدَامَنَا وَانْصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكَافِرِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA FAQAWWINAA A'LAA SIYAAMINAA WA QIYAAMINAA WA THABBIT AQDAAMANAA WANSURNAA A'LAL QAWMIL KAAFIREEN\nO Allah, (please do) grant us strength to observe fasting and practice acts of worship in this month, make our steps firm, and assist us against the unbelieving people.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ الْوَاحِدُ فَلَا وَلَدَ لَكَ، وَاَنْتَ الصَّمَدُ فَلَا شِبْهَ لَكَ، وَاَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ فَلَا يُعِزُّكَ شَيْءٌ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTAL WAAHIDU FALAA WALADA LAKA WA ANTAS SAMADU FALAA SHIBHA LAKA WA ANTAL A'ZEEZU FALAA YU'IZZUKA SHAY'\nO Allah, You are surely the One; therefore, You have not son. You are the eternally Besought of all; therefore, nothing is like You. You are the Almighty; therefore, nothing can overcome You.\nوَاَنْتَ الْغَنِيُّ وَاَنَا الْفَقِيْرُ، وَاَنْتَ الْمَوْلٰى وَاَنَا الْعَبْدُ\nWA ANTAL GHANIYYU WA ANAL FAQEERU WA ANTAL MAWLAA WA ANAL A'BD\nYou are the Self-sufficient while I am poor. You are the Master while I am (Your) slave.\nوَاَنْتَ الْغَفُوْرُ وَاَنَا الْمُذْنِبُ، وَاَنْتَ الرَّحِيْمُ وَاَنَا الْمُخْطِئُ\nWA ANTAL GHAFOORU WA ANAL MUDHNIBU WA ANTAR RAHEEMU WA ANAL MUKHTI'\nYou are the All-forgiving while I am sinful. You are the All-merciful while I am mistaken.\nوَاَنْتَ الْخَالِقُ وَاَنَا الْمَخْلُوْقُ، وَاَنْتَ الْحَيُّ وَاَنَا الْمَيِّتُ\nWA ANTAL KHAALIQU WA ANAL MAKHLOOQU WA ANTAL HAYYU WA ANAL MAYYIT\nYou are the Creator while I am (Your) creature. You are the Ever-living while I am mortal.\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ اَنْ تَغْفِرَ لِيْ وَتَرْحَمَنِيْ، وَتَجَاوَزَ عَنِّي اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nAS'ALUKA BIRAHMATIKA AN TAGHFIRA LEE WA TARHAMANEE WA TAJAAWAZA A'NNEE INNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nI thus beseech You in the name of Your mercy to forgive me, have mercy upon me, and excuse my offenses. You have power over all things.",
    "Reciting the Quran\nRecite the Holy Quran often in the first hours of Ramazan. Before you begin, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اَشْهَدُ اَنَّ هٰذَا كِتَابُكَ الْمُنْزَلُ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِكَ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَبْدِاللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASH-HADU ANNA HAADHAA KITAABUKAL MUNZALU MIN I'NDIKA A'LAA RASOOLIKA MUHAMMADIBNI A'BDILLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nO Allah, I testify that this is the Book revealed by You on Your Messenger Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah, blessings of Allah be on him and on his Household\nوَكَلَامُكَ النَّاطِقُ عَلٰى لِسَانِ نَبِيِّكَ، جَعَلْتَهٗ هَادِيًا مِنْكَ اِلٰى خَلْقِكَ، وَحَبْلًا مُتَّصِلًا فِيْمَا بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ عِبَادِكَ\nWA KALAAMUKAN NAATIQU A'LAA LISAANI NABIYYIKA JA'ALTAHOO HAADIYAN MINKA ILAA KHALQIKA WA HABLAN MUTTASILAN FEEMAA BAYNAKA WA BAYNA I'BAADIK\n(these are) Your Words, Your Prophet gave tongue to, (whom) You appointed as guide for the people, and a connected link between You and Your servants.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي نَشَرْتُ عَهْدَكَ وَكِتابَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE NASHARTU A'HDAKA WA KITAABAK\nO Allah, I am opening Your testament and Your Book.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاجْعَلْ نَظَرِيْ فِيْهِ عِبَادَةً، وَقِرَاۤءَتِي فِيْهِ فِكْرًا، وَفِكْرِيْ فِيْهِ اعْتِبَارًا\nALLAAHUMMA FAJ'AL NAZAREE FEEHI I'BAADATAN WA QIRAA'ATEE FEEHI FIKRAN WA FIKREE FEEHI'TIBAARAA\nO Allah, decide my looking in it to be a kind of worship, my reciting in it to be ponderation, and my ponderation over it to be learning lessons from it.\nوَاجْعَلْنِيْ مِمَّنْ اِتَّعَظَ بِبَيَانِ مَوَاعِظِكَ فِيْهِ، وَاجْتَنَبَ مَعَاصِيْكَ\nWAJ'ALNEE MIMMAN ITTA'AZA BIBAYAANI MAWAA'IZIKA FEEHI WAJTANABA MA'AASEEK\nInclude me with those who take lessons from the elucidation of Your preaches therein and those who accordingly avoid doing acts of disobedience to You.\nوَلَا تَطْبَعْ عِنْدَ قِرَاۤءَتِيْ عَلٰى سَمْعِيْ، وَلَا تَجْعَلْ عَلٰى بَصَرِيْ غِشَاوَةً، وَلَا تَجْعَلْ قِرَاۤءَتِي قِرَاۤءَةً لَا تَدَبُّرَ فِيْهَا\nWA LAA TATBA' I'NDA QIRAA'ATEE A'LAA SAM'EE WA LAA TAJ'AL A'LAA BASAREE GHISHAAWATAN WA LAA TAJ'AL QIRAA'ATEE QIRAA'ATAN LAA TADABBURA FEEHAA\nDo not seal on my hearing while I am reciting it, do not place covering on my sight, and do not decide my reciting to be thoughtless\nبَلِ اجْعَلْنِيْ اَتَدَبَّرُ اٰيَاتِهٖ وَاَحْكَامَهٗ، اٰخِذًا بِشَرَايِعِ دِيْنِكَ\nBALIJ A'LNEE ATADABBARU AAYAATIHEE WA AHKAAMAHOO AAKHIDHAN BISHARAAYI'I DEENIK\nrather, (please) make me ponder over its verses and laws, learning the laws of my religion.\nوَلَا تَجْعَلْ نَظَرِيْ فِيْهِ غَفْلَةً، وَلَا قِرَاۤءَتِيْ هَذَرًا\nWA LAA TAJ'AL NAZAREE FEEHI GHAFLATAN WA LAA QIRAA'ATEE HADHARAA\nDo not decide my looking in it to be inadvertence, and do not allow my reciting to be worthless.\nاِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الرَّؤُوْفُ الرَّحِيْمُ\nINNAKA ANTAR RA'OOFUR RAHEEM\nYou are verily the All-kind, the All-merciful.\nWhen you finish, recite [Dua after Reciting the Holy Quran](A2)."
  ],
  "merits": "Intercourse with one's wife is otherwise discommended on the first night of the Arabic months; this exception is one of the peculiarities of the holy month of Ramadan.\n\nGhusl: A Hadith reads that if one washes himself at the first night of Ramadan, one will be secured against prurigo up to the next Ramadan. Bathing in a flowing river and pouring thirty handfuls of water on the head keeps one mentally pure up to the next Ramadan.\n\nZiyarat: Visiting the holy tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) on this night brings forgiveness of sins and the like of the reward of those who undertake Hajj and 'Umrah in that year.\n\nAllahumma Inna Hadha al-Shahr al-Mubarak: This supplication is also among the rites of the last night of Sha'ban.\n\nDua Ya Man Yamliku al-Tadbir: Reported in al-Iqbal from Imam Muhammad al-Jawad al-Taqi (a.s.).\n\nAllahumma Rabba Shahri Ramadan: Reported from Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.), as mentioned in the book of al-Iqbal.\n\nAllahumma Inna Hadha Shahru Ramadan: Sayyid Ibn Tawus records this in Iqbal al-A'mal, from a book of supplications in the handwriting of al-Sharif al-Radi, to be said when the month of Ramadan arrives.\n\nAllahumma Hadha Shahru Ramadan al-Mubarak: Sayyid Ibn Tawus records this in Iqbal al-A'mal through Harun ibn Musa al-Tal'ukbari from Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.), to be said when the month of Ramadan arrives. It may be said on the first night or on the first day; Ibn Tawus preferred the first day. Said at night, mention \"this night of mine\" before \"this day of mine\".\n\nDuas of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.): According to a Hadith, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) used to say the first of these at the beginning of Ramadan, and is also reported to have said the second at the first night of Ramadan.\n\nReciting the Quran: Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) used to say this supplication before he would start reciting the Holy Qur'an, and [Dua after Reciting the Holy Quran](A2) when he finished."
}
